## OpenPlanr host-native workflows

OpenPlanr semantic work runs in the active coding session. It does not launch a
second model or require provider API keys.

- `{{specInvocation}} <intent-or-SPEC>` shapes product intent into a specification.
- `{{planInvocation}} <SPEC>` authors implementation-ready stories and tasks directly.
- `{{shipInvocation}} <task-or-request>` implements and verifies local repository work.

Use the host's native structured question surface when a material decision cannot
be inferred. Use `planr` only for deterministic storage, inspection, validation,
rendering, serving, setup, and synchronization utilities.
